WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.850
Follow a harvest: from
a field, onto a lorry,

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.650
into a shop, and into a kitchen.

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:13.630
In 2022, UNEP estimated 1.05
billion tonnes of food waste.

4
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.750
That's almost one-fifth of all
food available to consumers.

5
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.890
And 132 kilograms for every person.

6
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.230
So where does so much go missing?

7
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.210
On the farm?

8
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.410
In storage?

9
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.030
In shops and restaurants?

10
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.650
In our own homes?

11
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.490
In this mission, you'll map
feeding the world as a system,

12
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.870
from inputs and growing to waste disposal.

13
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.870
Then you'll sort farming
from intensive to extensive,

14
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.590
and subsistence to commercial.

15
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.250
Your mission: find out where so much of the
world's food goes missing on the journey

16
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.010
from field to fork.
